{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\to M$", "MATH_0002": "$U/R$", "MATH_0003": "$U/R \\to M$", "MATH_0004": "$U/R \\to M$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a1865aa6ef9b7e52c4b7d8165b4f028e2c6348fe821a0ee1336a78c72439c37a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5fc5e418c10079d5529a76e15bcb665b5f8d6b81def08eac3fb4ceb3df874fa8", "source_text": "Condition (1) says that <MATH_0001> factors through <MATH_0002>.\nCondition (2) says that <MATH_0003> is surjective as a map of sheaves.\nCondition (3) says that <MATH_0004> is injective as a map of sheaves.\nHence the lemma follows.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ae939baf572e859ab667f4c0c1e48f3446580f032c00bec2cb612bb51d7a24c4", "unit_id": "tag:044M:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1f3b8144e752d23826950d22937ea376cf428d85c0877eee4198d32536dff478", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cecb8dc779dc97cd66cfc1f46cf670252abbdfd41aea03496a5bc7c1e5e22c60", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma is wrong if we do not require <MATH_0001> to be a\npre-equivalence relation (but just a pre-relation say).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4ff290b5563a614c44f64596619efef90f59723b7518cd7b86139e27de3209eb", "unit_id": "tag:044H:prose-0004"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$S'$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$a, b \\in U(S')$", "MATH_0009": "$a$", "MATH_0010": "$b$", "MATH_0011": "$(U/R)(S')$", "MATH_0012": "$\\{f_i : S_i \\to S'\\}$", "MATH_0013": "$S'$", "MATH_0014": "$r_i : S_i \\to R$", "MATH_0015": "$a \\circ f_i = s \\circ r_i$", "MATH_0016": "$b \\circ f_i = t \\circ r_i$", "MATH_0017": "$$\nR \\longrightarrow U \\times_{U/R} U\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quotient-pre-equivalence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d2a1d4c813cccd613f88c4197c28a705bb941fd1a89ea339e81b70fd51a6f5c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e575a968b4b1e8099d4c9bbfcc5c9146cc4d477c2de20dec2fcdfd06aa108ad0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-equivalence relation over <MATH_0005>.\nFor a scheme <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007> and <MATH_0008> the following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010> map to the same element of <MATH_0011>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> there exists an fppf covering <MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013>\nand morphisms <MATH_0014> such that\n<MATH_0015> and <MATH_0016>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\nIn other words, in this case the map of sheaves\n<MATH_0017>\nis surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:45e5b72f2023c72828d80cea9606409349cf18ca4e0bf35eea0f306e5b5a1a82", "unit_id": "tag:046O:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T \\mapsto U(T)/j(R(T))$", "MATH_0002": "$j(R(T)) \\subset U(T) \\times U(T)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-quotient-presheaf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-equivalence-relation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dd58a687a9b6bad4699a2bb9853f477043c9d6c1948554db9b368997721ab11d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a21117ab388c3e1990caba1589e2e5b2cefbfee361bdce5c91b61dd3d42de469", "source_text": "Omitted. Hint: The reason this works is that the presheaf\n(<REF_0001>) in this case is really given\nby <MATH_0001> as <MATH_0002>\nis an equivalence relation, see\nDefinition <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:367e42a9af7563b721d373abed597c241cb56d6e967502106d3a2296c1eb12ca", "unit_id": "tag:046O:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$g : U' \\to U$", "MATH_0007": "$B$", "MATH_0008": "$j' : R' \\to U' \\times_B U'$", "MATH_0009": "$j$", "MATH_0010": "$U'$", "MATH_0011": "$$\nU'/R' \\longrightarrow U/R\n$$", "MATH_0012": "$U' \\to U$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{g : U' \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0014": "$U'/R' \\to U/R$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-topologies-definition-fppf-covering}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-quotient-pre-equivalence-relation-restrict}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:96914900da4e842ff859202a45f9283d09ebf25655287232b730bf8cc72bd44c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:49d4ca778e66c17e38aeeb206619d3782570be8aea0a6c51873c66baf5273a29", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-equivalence relation over <MATH_0005>\nand <MATH_0006> a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0007>.\nLet <MATH_0008> be the restriction of <MATH_0009> to <MATH_0010>.\nThe map of quotient sheaves\n<MATH_0011>\nis injective. If <MATH_0012> is surjective as a map of sheaves, for\nexample if <MATH_0013> is an fppf covering (see\nTopologies on Spaces,\nDefinition <REF_0001>),\nthen <MATH_0014> is an isomorphism of sheaves.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7afa960ee24da62bb8ec49ca0a6093cfd56d4def65406a5909fc17e5595fb071", "unit_id": "tag:046P:statement"}
